# Approach 1:

## Time Complexity: O(nlogn)
## Space COmplexity: O(1)

```
class Solution {
    public int maxProduct(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        Arrays.sort(nums);

        return ((nums[n - 1] - 1) * (nums[n - 2] - 1));
    }
}
```

# Approach 2:

## Time Complexity: O(n)
## Space COmplexity: O(1)

```
class Solution {
    public int maxProduct(int[] nums) {
        int n = nums.length;
        int max1 = 1;
        int max2 = 1;

        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            if (max1 < nums[i]) {
                max2 = max1;
                max1 = nums[i];
            } else if (max2 < nums[i]) {
                max2 = nums[i];
            }
        }

        return (max1 - 1) * (max2 - 1);
    }
}
```
